# Claude Opus 5 — findings by Iceman

- Source: Anthropic/Claude Opus 5
- Date: 2026-11-10 (UTC)
- Overview and scoring methodology: `../../model-comparison.md`
- Cross-model signed log: `../../model-findings.md`

## Model card

- **Name:** Claude Opus 5
- **Short description:** Anthropic’s Claude Opus 5 is a legacy Opus-tier model (released July 24, 2026) for long autonomous coding and knowledge work, succeeded by Claude Opus 5.5. Public materials emphasize strong efficiency and agentic performance, but independently extractable benchmark numbers were limited in this pass.
- **Provider / access:** Anthropic Claude API `claude-opus-5`; available on Bedrock, Google Cloud, Microsoft Foundry, and Claude Platform on AWS per platform docs. No confirmed OpenCode Zen Free ID (`noFreeId` in local metadata).
- **Release / knowledge:** Released July 24, 2026 (platform docs/announcement). Reliable knowledge cutoff May 2026; training data cutoff May 2026.
- **IDs:** `claude-opus-5`, `anthropic.claude-opus-5` (Bedrock). Local metadata ID `anthropic/claude-opus-5`.
- **Context window:** 1M tokens context, 128K max output (300K batch beta supported per docs).
- **Modalities:** Text and image input; text output.
- **Pricing (as of 2026-11-10):** Paid tier — $5 / 1M input, $25 / 1M output (per docs/announcement); cache/batch pricing per Anthropic pricing.
- **Architecture:** Proprietary Anthropic model; architecture/parameter count not publicly disclosed.

